# Nordic palette for every fzf invocation. Read by the fzf binary itself through
# FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS_FILE, so it reaches the Ctrl-R/Ctrl-T widgets and fzf-tab's
# completion menus without either of them knowing about it.
#
# Colours are nordic.nvim, the same source as .config/ghostty/themes/nordic:
# #88C0D0 accent, #81A1C1 secondary, #3B4252 selection, #4C566A dimmed.
#
# Theme only -- no layout or behaviour, those stay with the caller. An invalid
# key makes fzf exit 2 rather than ignore the line, so a typo is loud.
#
# bg and gutter are deliberately unset: inside the § popup the background then
# comes from tmux's popup-style (#242933), and in a normal shell from ghostty's
# background. Naming one here paints a slightly different rectangle inside the
# popup instead. border matches popup-border-style, so fzf's preview separator
# lines up with the popup's own border.

--color=fg:#C0C8D8,fg+:#ECEFF4,hl:#88C0D0,hl+:#88C0D0
--color=bg+:#3B4252,gutter:-1
--color=prompt:#88C0D0,pointer:#88C0D0,marker:#A3BE8C,spinner:#B48EAD
--color=info:#81A1C1,border:#81A1C1,label:#81A1C1,separator:#3B4252,header:#4C566A
--color=query:#C0C8D8
